{
  "case_id": "2008-08-441",
  "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The court of appeals erred in holding that the plaintiff had to have direct evidence in order to obtain the specific instruction at issue in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Excuse me. That -- that statement may be wrong depending upon how you read Price Waterhouse, might it not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, but -- I just want -- you said that the Court has never imposed a burden of proof-shifting requirement absent a directive from Congress? Are you --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there a variety of views among the circuits on what Justice O'Connor meant by the term \"direct evidence\"? It wasn't defined in Price Waterhouse either."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, would the -- if there is a direct evidence requirement, it may arguably cause a great deal of problem when the trial judge has to give an instruction to the jury, because then the -- the jury will first have to decide whether a particular type of evidence is present in the case before it can tell what -- who has the burden of proof and what the standard is, but if Price Waterhouse is understood simply as a way for a judge conducting a bench trial to look at the evidence, does it present any of the problems that have been identified with the Price Waterhouse -- that interpretation of Price Waterhouse as applied to jury trials?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Am I right that the only source of argument for the proposition that it does have to be direct evidence is Justice O'Connor's opinion, separate opinion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could I ask you this? Do you think that there is a tenable distinction between a mixed motives case and a non-mixed motives case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. BLATT",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You could have what your view suggests, which is after summary judgment you could get a motivated factor instruction that the jury would be permitted to find both impermissible and permissible motives."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE ALITO",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there any -- is there any empirical evidence to show whether any of this really makes a difference. Have there been studies on the effect of the 1991 amendments, whether they have made a difference in the way cases actually come out?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. PHILLIPS",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It does seem to me in some ways the Petitioner and Respondent in this case are ships passing in the night because the issues here are unbelievably complicated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. PHILLIPS",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It played a part. It did have a role: Age motivated in part."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I mean -- in the first place, saying that something is a motivating factor or played a role is, as a sufficient basis on which to impose liability, is flatly inconsistent with what this Court has said numerous time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But Price Waterhouse deviated -- that was --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Will you --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: You -- pardon me?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Can I get back to Justice Stevens's hypothetical?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PHILLIPS: There -- there is no question about that. And it is -- again, the only question is: Who bears the burden of proof?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PHILLIPS: Well, there is a question about the adequacy of the jury instruction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Don't those cases involve two independent physical causes of an event, not the breaking down of human motivation into -- into separate factors?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Schnapper",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there is a long line of cases, including a number of decisions by Learned Hand in 1938, one which we have cited, Transportation Management, in which the lower courts have agreed that where multiple factors are involved it's reasonable to put the burden on the defendant which -- of sorting it all out."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "496d7a1cc4ac56d6db11bfb7190dc8e3437771070ae13d9c32df40fd8e64be2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-496d7a1cc4ac-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-08-441",
      "confidence": 0.0,
